  "question": {
    "text": "For natural numbers $m, n$ if $(1-y)^m(1+y)^n=1+a_1 y+a_2 y^2+\\ldots$, and $a_1=a_2=10$ then $(\\mathrm{m}, \\mathrm{n})$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4Ot3Z",
      "text": "\n(20, 45)\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nIlPP",
      "text": "\n(35, 20)\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6BwhM",
      "text": "\n(45, 35)\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fCjd9",
      "text": "\n(35, 45)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$(1-y)^m(1+y)^n=\\left[1-{ }^m C_1 y+{ }^m C_2 y^2-\\ldots\\right]\\left[1+{ }^n C_1 y+{ }^n C_2 y^2+\\ldots\\right]$\n$=1+(n-m)+\\left\\{\\frac{m(m-1)}{2}+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}-m n\\right\\} y^2+\\ldots .$.\n$\\therefore a_1=n-m=10$ and $a_2=\\frac{m^2+n-m-n-2 m n}{2}=10$\nSo, $n-m=10$ and $(m-n)^2-(m+n)=20 \\quad \\Rightarrow m+n=80$\n$$\n\\therefore \\mathrm{m}=35, \\quad \\mathrm{n}=45\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
